			<Placemark>
				<name>燃料混合处理</name>
				<LookAt>
					<longitude>125.7518662094573</longitude>
					<latitude>39.76875745319374</latitude>
					<altitude>0</altitude>
					<range>1091.011310079941</range>
					<tilt>2.660977528706102e-010</tilt>
					<heading>-1.268780606733153</heading>
				</LookAt>
				<styleUrl>#khStyle535_copy0</styleUrl>
				<Point>
					<coordinates>125.7499832101131,39.76956819308285,0</coordinates>
				</Point>
			</Placemark>
			<Placemark>
				<name>加工/实验室</name>
				<description><![CDATA[状态：部分完成。1987年开始建设,根据1994年的美国北韩框架协议于1994年停止. <br>
国际原子能机构安全保障:国际原子能机构监督工程冻结.<br>
扩散关注:<br>   1992年视察员发现该设施建成了80%和安装了40%的设备. 国际原子能机构的官员说它建得"非常原始的",远远不能以工业规模生产钚. <br><br>     注:朝鲜认为这个600ft长的设施是实验室设施,因为它从来没有全面调试,而且到1992年首次被国际原子能机构检查也没有完全建成. 但是,国际原子能机构坚持它是乏燃料后处理设施. <br>
原文如下：<br><hr>
Status: Partially completed. Construction began in 1987 and was halted in 1994 under terms of the 1994 US-North Korean Agreed Framework. <br><br>

IAEA safeguards: IAEA monitoring construction freeze. <br><br>

Proliferation Concern: <br>
In 1992, IAEA inspectors found the facility 80 percent constructed with 40 percent of the equipment installed. An IAEA official described the building as "extremely primitive" and far from ready to produce plutonium on an industrial scale. <br><br>

Note: North Korea maintains that the 600ft-long facility is a radiochemical laboratory because it has never been fully tested and when first inspected by the IAEA in 1992, was only partially completed. However, the IAEA insists that it is a spent fuel reprocessing facility.]]></description>
